// Formative practice quiz for controlled-forms. Low-stakes; answers are visible by design. First draft, not yet reviewed.
$CATEGORY: react/forms-context-and-crud/controlled-forms

::controlled-forms o1 - checkbox property::Which pair correctly controls a checkbox?{
=checked from state, and onChange reading e.target.checked#Correct. Checkboxes use the checked property.
~value from state, and onChange reading e.target.value#Not quite. For a checkbox, value is a fixed string, and it does not track ticking.
~defaultChecked and no handler#Not quite. That is uncontrolled, so state would not follow it.
~onClick only#Not quite. Without checked from state, the checkbox is not controlled.
}

::controlled-forms o1 - read the new text::Inside a text field onChange handler, where does the new text come from?{
=e.target.value#Correct. The event target is the input, and its value is the new text.
~The state variable#Not quite. State still holds the old value until after the setter runs.
~e.value#Not quite. The value is on the target, not on the event object.
~document.title#Not quite. That is the page title, which has nothing to do with this field.
}

::controlled-forms o2 - preventDefault::Why does a form onSubmit handler call event.preventDefault?{
=To stop the browser submitting the form and reloading the page#Correct. A reload would lose your app state, and you are handling submission in JavaScript.
~To clear all the fields#Not quite. It does not touch the fields.
~To validate the inputs#Not quite. It does no validation.
~To send the request#Not quite. It only stops the default. You still send the request yourself.
}

::controlled-forms o3 - value without onChange::An input has a value prop from state and no onChange. What does the user experience?{
=Typing appears to do nothing#Correct. State never changes, so React keeps showing the old value.
~Typing updates state automatically#Not quite. Only the setter updates state.
~The input becomes uncontrolled#Not quite. The value prop keeps it controlled.
~The value clears on every key#Not quite. It keeps the state value rather than clearing.
}

::controlled-forms o3 - defaultValue meaning::What does defaultValue do?{
=Sets only the initial text of an uncontrolled input#Correct. After that, the browser keeps the value.
~Keeps the input in sync with state on every render#Not quite. That is what value does.
~Resets the input on every keystroke#Not quite. It applies only at the start.
~Makes the input read-only#Not quite. That is the readOnly attribute.
}
